WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:03.489
Speaker 1: All right, we have so much to cover
today that I'm not even going to waste time

00:00:03.489 --> 00:00:08.260
talking about the world famous benefits of
membership, I'm going to skip that and jump

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:10.380
right into material because there's just too
much to cover.

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:15.110
And this is really interesting economically.

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:23.070
We have all over the map opinions about a
recent statement by Joe Biden about so-called

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:28.300
free riders on the unemployment insurance
enhanced unemployment insurance that is currently

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:32.140
available now for framing, for context.

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:39.550
Any social insurance program has the possibility
of free riders, people on food stamps who

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:41.149
shouldn't really get them.

00:00:41.149 --> 00:00:46.940
But they're using business expenses to artificially
lower their incomes so that they qualify for

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:52.309
food stamps or whatever, or people who choose
not to work or not work as much in order to

00:00:52.309 --> 00:00:58.300
qualify for Medicaid instead of working and
earning more and paying for their health insurance,

00:00:58.300 --> 00:00:59.300
for example.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:04.549
Now, no honest person who understands any
social insurance program will tell you that

00:01:04.549 --> 00:01:05.930
free riders don't exist.

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:07.359
They do exist.

00:01:07.359 --> 00:01:13.590
But the point is, when we think about macroeconomics
instead of the micro of such programs, if

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:18.990
the programs are finely tuned, if the benefits
are well calibrated, if the means testing

00:01:18.990 --> 00:01:24.649
is appropriate and enforced, assuming it's
a means tested program, you basically don't

00:01:24.649 --> 00:01:29.289
worry about a few anecdotal free riders because
they are relatively few.

00:01:29.289 --> 00:01:34.389
And the program overall at the societal level,
at the macroeconomic level is a positive thing

00:01:34.389 --> 00:01:35.389
for the economy.

00:01:35.389 --> 00:01:41.009
That's the general approach to any properly
administered social insurance program.

00:01:41.009 --> 00:01:46.930
Right now we do have a unique circumstances
with so-called enhanced unemployment benefits

00:01:46.930 --> 00:01:48.799
through the federal government during the
pandemic.

00:01:48.799 --> 00:01:53.829
Now, normally, unemployment insurance and
benefits are a state thing.

00:01:53.829 --> 00:01:56.309
States determine the level of benefits.

00:01:56.309 --> 00:01:57.399
They vary by state.

00:01:57.399 --> 00:02:00.579
They tend to be higher in states with higher
wages and higher cost of living.

00:02:00.579 --> 00:02:01.579
And that's fine.

00:02:01.579 --> 00:02:04.149
And that's how it all works in this case.

00:02:04.149 --> 00:02:08.379
And this is a very rare situation because
of the pandemic, the federal government came

00:02:08.379 --> 00:02:14.629
in and they dropped an enhancement on people,
in many cases disconnected from what they

00:02:14.629 --> 00:02:18.940
were earning in the job they lost due to the
pandemic.

00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:25.770
So you can always say there are some people
choosing unemployment insurance instead of

00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:27.150
working.

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:32.980
We don't worry about it because unemployment
insurance runs out.

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:35.129
The benefits aren't huge.

00:02:35.129 --> 00:02:40.180
There is not that many people who even could
earn more from the unemployment insurance

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:42.150
than from working.

00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:50.920
It's also just a truth about humans that people
generally want to feel useful and they want

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:51.920
to work.

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:56.609
So while sure, anecdotally, there might be
some people in normal circumstances that have

00:02:56.609 --> 00:03:01.359
figured out a way to earn the same or almost
the same from staying home, it's not really

00:03:01.359 --> 00:03:09.080
a macroeconomic concern in this particular
moment because of the enhanced federal unemployment,

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:16.129
there are more people who theoretically could
earn a little more from staying home and collecting

00:03:16.129 --> 00:03:20.890
the normal state unemployment benefits, plus
the enhanced federal benefits then from going

00:03:20.890 --> 00:03:25.220
back to the job that they had, that that is
theoretically possible right now and anecdotally

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:26.269
it's happening.

00:03:26.269 --> 00:03:31.470
So Joe Biden gave a series of remarks yesterday
on the economy and talked about how jobs numbers

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:34.670
from April were short of what was expected.

00:03:34.670 --> 00:03:39.280
And one reason that's being cited is that
because of this enhanced unemployment, there

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:45.359
are more people than usual turning down jobs
so that they can stay home and collect that

00:03:45.359 --> 00:03:47.140
sweet, sweet, enhanced unemployment.

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:49.489
So Joe Biden says he's going to deal with
that.

00:03:49.489 --> 00:03:50.840
Let's take a listen.

00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:54.989
Speaker 2: Look, fifth thing we're going to
do, we're going to make it clear that anyone

00:03:54.989 --> 00:04:03.180
collecting unemployment was offered a suitable
job must take the job or lose their unemployment

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:05.280
benefits.

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:11.290
There are a few covid-19 related exceptions
so that people aren't forced to choose between

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:13.849
their basic safety and a paycheck.

00:04:13.849 --> 00:04:15.730
But otherwise, that's the law.

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:19.930
Speaker 1: Now, there are already a ton of
things to talk about here.

00:04:19.930 --> 00:04:24.419
First of all, as Joe Biden says, this is already
the law.

00:04:24.419 --> 00:04:28.550
All of these unemployment systems in each
state, sometimes it's by phone, sometimes

00:04:28.550 --> 00:04:29.550
it's online.

00:04:29.550 --> 00:04:31.340
There's different ways that it's done.

00:04:31.340 --> 00:04:35.440
You regularly have to answer questions like,
are you looking for a job?

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:37.050
Did you apply for jobs?

00:04:37.050 --> 00:04:38.440
Have you been interviewed?

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:40.780
Were you offered a job that you turned down?

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:44.110
So Joe Biden is not creating any new law here.

00:04:44.110 --> 00:04:48.530
Joe Biden is saying we're going to enforce
the rules on unemployment.

00:04:48.530 --> 00:04:49.750
Interesting.

00:04:49.750 --> 00:04:52.270
It's really difficult to enforce.

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:53.780
People are self reporting.

00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:57.310
There's relatively little confirmation or
oversight.

00:04:57.310 --> 00:04:59.060
There's no central database.

00:04:59.060 --> 00:05:03.139
Where the government could determine you said
you weren't offered any jobs, but you were

00:05:03.139 --> 00:05:07.490
offered one and you declined it, it's basically
the honor system.

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:11.199
So this is really just kind of like a message
from Joe Biden.

00:05:11.199 --> 00:05:15.090
I don't really know how much will be done
as a result of it.

00:05:15.090 --> 00:05:16.639
But let's listen to a little bit more.

00:05:16.639 --> 00:05:22.730
Speaker 2: I know there's been a lot of discussion
since Friday, since Friday's report that people

00:05:22.730 --> 00:05:26.320
are being paid to stay home rather than go
to work.

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:29.979
Well, we don't see much evidence of that.

00:05:29.979 --> 00:05:32.580
That is a major factor.

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:35.220
We don't see that.

00:05:35.220 --> 00:05:42.630
Look, it's easy to say the line has been because
of the generous unemployment benefits.

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:46.050
That is a major factor in labor shortages.

00:05:46.050 --> 00:05:48.350
Americans want to work.

00:05:48.350 --> 00:05:53.780
Americans want to work, as my dad used to
say, jobs about a lot more than a paycheck.

00:05:53.780 --> 00:05:58.340
It's about your dignity, your place in the
community, being able to look your kid the

00:05:58.340 --> 00:06:00.910
eye and say everything's going to be OK.

00:06:00.910 --> 00:06:07.400
I think the people who claim Americans won't
work, even if they find a good and fair opportunity,

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:10.039
underestimate the American people.

00:06:10.039 --> 00:06:15.460
So we'll insist that the law is followed with
respect to benefits, but we're not going to

00:06:15.460 --> 00:06:18.509
turn our backs on our fellow Americans.

00:06:18.509 --> 00:06:26.889
22 million people lost their jobs in this
pandemic through no fault of their own.

00:06:26.889 --> 00:06:33.120
They lost their jobs to a virus and to a government
that bungled its response to the crisis and

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:35.270
failed to protect them.

00:06:35.270 --> 00:06:38.759
We still have eight million fewer jobs than
we did when the pandemic started.

00:06:38.759 --> 00:06:40.550
Speaker 1: OK, so you get the idea.

00:06:40.550 --> 00:06:42.810
So there have been two reactions to this.

00:06:42.810 --> 00:06:45.460
One reaction has been great.

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:48.280
Get these freeloaders off of unemployment.

00:06:48.280 --> 00:06:52.310
You have restaurants, you have other businesses
that can't find workers.

00:06:52.310 --> 00:06:57.190
So the story goes because people are happier
staying home and making enhanced unemployment

00:06:57.190 --> 00:06:58.800
rather than going back into work.

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:02.189
The reality is this is statistically rare.

00:07:02.189 --> 00:07:04.919
It's possible because of enhanced unemployment.

00:07:04.919 --> 00:07:07.139
There are anecdotes about it.

00:07:07.139 --> 00:07:14.159
But I worry that by even doing this, Joe Biden
is buying into this right wing narrative that

00:07:14.159 --> 00:07:18.439
we have no particular reason to except we
don't have to accept that right wing narrative.

00:07:18.439 --> 00:07:22.199
But there's another side to this which many
people are reacting with.

00:07:22.199 --> 00:07:29.550
If the wages are so low at these jobs that
you do make more staying home on unemployment.

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:34.889
Isn't that a sign that maybe the wages are
too low, raise the wages in order to attract

00:07:34.889 --> 00:07:35.889
employees?

00:07:35.889 --> 00:07:42.590
Now, remember, this is not normally as much
of an issue when there is not the enhanced

00:07:42.590 --> 00:07:43.590
unemployment.

00:07:43.590 --> 00:07:45.520
This is really a transient issue.

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:48.810
Enhanced unemployment from the federal government
is going to be ending in all likelihood later

00:07:48.810 --> 00:07:50.080
this year.

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:53.379
But what does it say about the wages being
paid?

00:07:53.379 --> 00:07:58.889
Another practical difficulty is Biden says,
you know, you can't turn down a suitable job

00:07:58.889 --> 00:08:01.240
and continue to collect unemployment.

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:02.539
Who determines if it's suitable?

00:08:02.539 --> 00:08:07.819
If you lost a job making sixty five thousand
dollars and you're offered one making thirteen

00:08:07.819 --> 00:08:10.889
dollars an hour, is that suitable?

00:08:10.889 --> 00:08:14.690
Do you lose unemployment benefits if you don't
accept that job?

00:08:14.690 --> 00:08:17.650
So I think that this is basically unenforceable.

00:08:17.650 --> 00:08:20.419
I'm curious to see what enforcement there
will be.

00:08:20.419 --> 00:08:25.020
I think enhanced unemployment is going to
end before there is any real enforcement.

00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:30.789
And much of the problem is that I see Joe
Biden by doing this as playing into a Republican

00:08:30.789 --> 00:08:33.670
criticism, which is barely valid.

00:08:33.670 --> 00:08:38.570
Again, any social insurance program, anecdotally,
you can find instances of anything.

00:08:38.570 --> 00:08:43.650
The question is, at a macro level, is that
actually a drag on the program?

00:08:43.650 --> 00:08:49.500
Enhanced unemployment has been a huge saving
grace for so many people.

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:52.140
And my concern is Biden's just buying into
it too much.

00:08:52.140 --> 00:08:55.700
And it's not really the problem that Republicans
claim it to be.

00:08:55.700 --> 00:08:56.460
Let me know what you think

